PART 6 — DEG/EG CONVERTER: PER-GLYCOL INDEPENDENCE (CRITICAL, PRODUCTION BLOCKER)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

BUG (unresolved for days): Polysorbate 80 shows DEG=Yes + EG=Yes when only 
EG is tested. Croda CoA tests ONLY Ethylene Glycol (USP <469>), NOT DEG. 
Confirmed the fault is in the ANNEXURE CONVERTER (vision extraction), which 
infers DEG from the "USP <469>" chapter reference because <469> covers both 
glycols by title.

Fix — TWO layers, both required:

6A — Converter prompt (deg_eg_annexure_converter.py), add PER-GLYCOL 
INDEPENDENCE block, highest priority instruction:

"DEG and EG are SEPARATE compounds. Evaluate each INDEPENDENTLY. NEVER copy 
one glycol's evidence to the other. A CoA testing ONLY Ethylene Glycol 
(e.g. 'Ethylene Glycol NMT 620 ppm PASS' or 'ETHYLENE GLYCOL (USP/NF 469) 
620 PPM MAX') is EG=Yes but DEG=Unknown. The mention of 'USP <469>' or 
'USP/NF 469' (whose chapter title names both glycols) does NOT authorize a 
DEG value when no explicit Diethylene Glycol numeric line is printed. Only an 
explicit 'Diethylene Glycol' line with its own numeric limit makes DEG=Yes.

Case A — only EG printed:
  deg_present=Unknown, deg_source=not_mentioned, deg_specification_limit=null
  eg_present=Yes, eg_source=vendor_coa, eg_specification_limit='NMT 620 ppm'
Case B — only DEG printed: mirror image.
Case C — both printed: both Yes with their OWN limits.
Case D — 'USP <469> compliant' with no per-glycol number: both Unknown.
NEVER emit the same numeric limit for both glycols from a single-glycol line."

6B — Post-processing guard in process_deg_eg_annexure (deterministic 
backstop, product-agnostic):

For each glycol independently, if present=="Yes":
  Check raw_text contains that glycol's OWN name near a numeric ppm/PASS 
  (word-boundary match: "diethylene glycol"/"deg" vs 
   "(?<!di)(?<!tri)ethylene glycol"/"eg").
  If the specific glycol name + numeric evidence is NOT found in raw_text 
  (only the OTHER glycol's is), downgrade:
    present="Unknown", specification_limit=null, source="not_mentioned"
  Log: "Downgraded {glycol} to Unknown for {material}: no explicit 
       {glycol} evidence; USP<469> reference alone insufficient."

6C — Downstream build_assessment (deg_eg.py) — already correct per prior 
review (per-glycol render). Verify it consumes the corrected per-glycol 
fields and renders DEG row and EG row from their OWN limits (never shared).

Acceptance:
  Polysorbate 80 (Croda CoA): Table 2 DEG=No, EG=Yes, spec="EG: NMT 620 ppm".
  Table 3: DEG row NA/NA/NA; EG row NA/620/620.
  Observations mention ONLY Ethylene Glycol as confirmed present.
  Mavacamten Mannitol (guarantee ceiling both): DEG=No/<1000, EG=No/<620, 
  both from their own declaration lines.
  Regression: Esomeprazole other excipients No/No/Not applicable.

